# Copy this to `hooks.cfg` next to hookdll.dll on the XP box to override
# which hooks are enabled / exit-hooked, without a rebuild. Not required --
# if hooks.cfg is missing, the built-in defaults apply (every confirmed
# address enabled with entry+exit, EXCEPT: the two `approximate: true`
# addresses -- fugc_mode_dispatch, tlb_f135_poly_remap -- disabled until
# you've verified them live; and tlb_polypixel, disabled by default for a
# DIFFERENT reason -- see below). See ../README.md for the full hook table
# and per-address citations.
#
# Syntax:
#   # comment
#   EXIT=on|off              global default for entry+exit vs entry-only
#   <hook_id>=on|off          enable/disable one hook entirely
#   <hook_id>.exit=on|off     entry+exit vs entry-only for one hook
#
# Example: the two approximate-address hooks are OFF by default -- if
# you've confirmed fugc_mode_dispatch's real entry address from a live
# disassembly on the XP box and want to try it:
#
# fugc_mode_dispatch=on

# Example: tla_colneg_mmx_kernel is described in its own citation as "the
# inner MMX kernel itself" -- if a first live run shows it firing at high
# frequency (large log volume / noticeable slowdown), turn off just its
# exit-hooking (keeps entry markers, drops the return-address-swap
# overhead), or disable it entirely:
#
# tla_colneg_mmx_kernel.exit=off
# tla_colneg_mmx_kernel=off

# tlb_polypixel is OFF by default (unlike everything else that isn't
# `approximate: true`) -- NOT because its address is in doubt (docs/74
# SS32.2 disassembled it directly: a completely ordinary, safe-to-hook
# function), but because it's a confirmed real per-pixel hot path AND the
# live-capture question it was originally hooked to answer (a naming
# ambiguity with tlb_f135_poly_remap) has since been fully resolved by
# that same static disassembly -- see hookcore_real_table.c's citation for
# the full reasoning. If you have a NEW reason to trace it live, turn on
# just entry markers first, not full entry+exit:
#
# tlb_polypixel=on
# tlb_polypixel.exit=off
